        "id": 2020502
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T07:30:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be acceptable to move the vector of UHIDDevice\u003cFile\u003e out of uhid.rs, as different usage may need to store different data with UHID device?",
      "parentUuid": "30103f20_3e16fa0b",
      "revId": "5f37fd4ee48cecd9ae6072e285535842fdff3118",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3fc44676_622205de",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 2020502
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T15:29:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Read function of `uhid-virt` can not be used directly as it is a synchronous function and need to be run from a blocking thread. In addition the underlying File is not public and `uhid-vrt` doesn\u0027t implement the clone trait.\n\niiuc the UHid struct in uhid.rs is just a list of UHIDDevice\u003cFile\u003e objects, allowing to destroy all of them with clear() method, without support to send/receive events from UHID or use a specific UHID device.\nAnd suspend.rs create an entry for each adapter on suspend.\nDo I understand it correctly?\n\nWhile for HFP, I rewrote the UHIDDevice\u003cFile\u003e to be able to clone the underlying File, which allows to send events from the main thread and wait for incoming event in a blocking thread.\n\nAs they have not the same purpose, I don\u0027t see how to merge them.\nWould it be ok if I move the UHidHfp cote from uhid_hfp.rs into uhid.rs?",
      "parentUuid": "0fd745e2_cb8da13d",
      "revId": "5f37fd4ee48cecd9ae6072e285535842fdff3118",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
